# VCP (Vauban Customer Portal)

Customer-facing web portal for **Vauban** (sibling of the
bastion product in `../Vauban`). This repository is **not** the bastion
admin UI (`vauban-web`); do not import bastion IPC, proxy, privsep, or
bastion Casbin policy files unless the user explicitly asks.

Project short name: **VCP**. Use that name in paths, crates, package
scopes, and commit/PR titles unless a longer form is clearer.

## Purpose

Internet-facing **CRUD customer portal** (HTTPS request/response — no
WebSocket product surface). Product IA is defined by
`.cursor/mockups/Concept/` and the `vcp` app route tree.

### Client zone (org-scoped)

- **Dashboard** — build / issues summary and recent activity
- **Documentation** — searchable knowledge base
- **Builds** — certified LTS/Stable/EOL binaries, signed download
- **Issues** — support tracker (SLA: initial analysis 2–5 business days)
- **Account & subscription** — plan, LTS counters, technical contact

### Admin zone (org-scoped, Casbin-gated)

- **Documentation editor** — write / publish / unpublish articles
- **Release manager** — publish binaries that appear in Builds
- **Client companies** — onboard orgs (`org.max_accounts_per_org`, default 5);
  account emails syntax-validated via Topcoat `Mailbox`

Security bar on the wire matches the bastion for **TLS 1.3** and
**post-quantum hybrid readiness** (`tls-post-quantum.mdc`), without
importing bastion IPC / privsep.

Prefer thin vertical slices over speculative features (no PSP checkout
until explicitly planned).

## Relationship to other repos

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `../Vauban` | Bastion product (Rust, Axum, Askama, …) |
| `../vauban.sh` | Public marketing site |
| **this repo** | Authenticated customer portal |

Share brand signals with `vauban.sh` / Concept mockups when designing UI;
do not copy bastion-internal dashboard patterns blindly.

## Working agreements

- Chat with the user in **French**; code, commits, and Markdown docs in
  **U.S. English** (see `markdown-us-english.mdc`, `git-workflow.mdc`).
- Never commit or push without explicit user authorization.
- Prefix diagnostic Shell commands with `rtk` (`rtk-proxy.mdc`).
- Version all of `.cursor/` (rules, skills, plans, audits) except
  `.cursor/mockups/` (local design artifacts only; see `.gitignore`).
- Stack conventions: `web-stack` skill; Topcoat framework knowledge:
  `topcoat` skill; authZ: `casbin-permissions.mdc`; dates:
  `timezone-localization.mdc`; tests: `vcp-test-pyramid.mdc`; TLS/PQ:
  `tls-post-quantum.mdc`.

## Stack status

**Topcoat** ([tokio-rs/topcoat](https://github.com/tokio-rs/topcoat)) —
Rust full-stack, server-rendered `view!`, optional signals / shards /
procedures, Tailwind + Topcoat UI. Early-stage: expect upstream breaking
changes; pin versions and prefer thin vertical slices.

**ORM / DB:** [Toasty](https://github.com/tokio-rs/toasty) +
**PostgreSQL** (pinned 0.x; see `web-stack` skill). Binary crate: `vcp`.

**Config:** TOML under `config/` (Vauban-style layering). No application
`.env`. Production is self-contained `config/vcp.conf` (deployed as
`/usr/local/etc/vcp/vcp.conf`). Local: `VCP_ENVIRONMENT=development`.
